  "instructions": [
    "Soak the rice noodles in a large bowl of hot tap water for 15 to 20 minutes, until bendy but still firm. Drain well.",
    "Whisk the tamari, fish sauce, brown sugar, rice vinegar, lime juice, and red pepper flakes in a small bowl until the sugar dissolves.",
    "Heat 1 tbsp oil in a 12-inch skillet over medium-high heat. Add the shrimp and cook 2 minutes per side, until pink and curled. Move them to a plate.",
    "Add 1 tbsp oil and the garlic to the skillet. Cook 30 seconds, then pour in the eggs and scramble until just set, about 1 minute.",
    "Add the remaining 1 tbsp oil, the drained noodles, and the sauce. Toss for 3 to 4 minutes, until the noodles are tender and have soaked up the sauce.",
    "Return the shrimp to the pan with the bean sprouts and half of the green onions. Toss 1 minute, until the shrimp are hot and opaque.",
    "Serve topped with the peanuts, the remaining green onions, and lime wedges."
  ],
